From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:43:22 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/72] runner: close frees the graph bank's prepared templates
 at engine close

The in-model runner was never freed: every bank template a cell prepared
lazily, and the runner's load blocks, stayed until exit and were reported
as leaks at SIGTERM (DSV41 rank 0: 64-372 extra blocks, 0.4-1.2 GB).

runner_open.close frees a runner's backends with their jobs, then the bank
(with every prepared template) and the circuit it loaded. The CUDA and
DSV41 engine closes call it after the engine thread stops, S3's runner
first since it shares the cells runner's circuit and bank. An idle unload
now drops the server's S3 executor at park and takes the reloaded engine's
at reload, so it never runs on a closed engine's runner.
